Reject ``bool`` arguments to :class:`vInt <icalendar.prop.integer.vInt>` with a clear :class:`TypeError`. Previously, ``vInt(True)`` and ``vInt(False)`` were silently accepted and stored as ``1`` and ``0`` respectively, which is almost always a bug (the caller likely wanted :class:`vBoolean <icalendar.prop.boolean.vBoolean>`, or the value was unboxed from JSON and the truthiness was incidental). The new error message names the offending type, includes the value, and points at ``vBoolean`` so the user can pick the right type without grepping the source.
